  data:  # fd14
    kind: work_item  # fd14
    title: "auto-pr --tracker-id runs a tracker mutation INSIDE its own PR_PENDING gate; auto-sync waits 15 min for the file auto-pr holds, then skips the sync (LIVE rule 19 shape)"  # fd14
    status: todo_hard  # fd14
    priority: 2  # fd14
    parent:  # fd14
    tags:  # fd14
    - tracker  # fd14
    - ci  # fd14
    isbefore: []  # fd14
    duplicate_of: []  # fd14
    not_duplicate_of: []  # fd14
    pr_ref:  # fd14
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 on PR #743 (WI-suhug), by watching auto-pr sit silent for 15 minutes after \"Note attached\".\n\nSHAPE (LIVE rule 19: a gate can block the work that would activate the mechanism it gates). `auto-pr --tracker-id X` appends a discussion to X AFTER the merge but BEFORE it removes `.git/PR_PENDING`. That `tracker discuss` runs `_maybe_auto_sync`; the pending ops were over the threshold (94 > 80), so it wanted to sync -- and `_maybe_auto_sync` (cli.py ~3116) sees `PR_PENDING`, prints \"auto-pr in flight, waiting\", and polls for up to `_SYNC_PR_WAIT_TIMEOUT` = 15 minutes for the file to clear. auto-pr is the process that will clear it, and it is blocked on the child. Observed: child `hypergumbo-tracker discuss WI-suhug... Merged as PR #743` in hrtimer_nanosleep for 900 s with no subprocess, then the sync is SKIPPED (not run), the discuss returns, auto-pr proceeds. Every `--tracker-id` run whose pending ops are over the threshold pays 15 minutes and then does NOT sync.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT A RACE BUT A DESIGN COLLISION. Both gates are correct on their own: the tracker must not merge a sync PR under a feature PR mid-CI (dev would advance under the feature branch), and auto-pr must hold PR_PENDING until its post-merge reconcile is done. The collision is that auto-pr performs a tracker MUTATION inside its own gate.\n\nFIX OPTIONS (pick one; the second touches a governance file):\n  (a) tracker package, non-governance: `_maybe_auto_sync` reads `PR_PENDING`'s content (auto-pr writes its own PID / PR number there -- verify) and, when the holder is an ANCESTOR of the current process (walk /proc ppid chain, or compare the PID in the file), SKIPS the wait immediately with a one-line notice (\"auto-pr is my caller; it will sync after it exits\" -- it will not, but the next mutation will). No 15-minute stall; the ops stay pending and journalled.\n  (b) scripts/auto-pr (governance -- needs_human_review): move the `--tracker-id` discuss to AFTER `rm .git/PR_PENDING` (the reconcile's last step), so the mutation runs ungated and auto-sync can fire normally. Cleaner, because it also lets the sync actually happen.\nEither way, pin it: a test that runs `_maybe_auto_sync` with PR_PENDING present and the holder being the test's own parent must return in < 1 s.\n\nCOST TODAY: 15 minutes per --tracker-id run over the threshold (three of today's runs), and a sync that silently does not happen -- the pending ops then ride on the NEXT mutation.\n\nSECOND FINDING, SAME RUN. After the 15-minute stall auto-pr reached its post-merge `git pull`, which failed on the known LIVE-s5 landmine (incoming tracker-sync commits carry ops files that are still pending locally: \"Your local changes ... would be overwritten\" + \"untracked working tree files would be overwritten\"), printed \"Git pull failed (attempt 1/3)\" and then reached `read -p \"Retry? [Y/n]\" -n 1 -r REPLY` -- an interactive prompt. Run detached (setsid nohup; stdin not a tty) the log shows NOTHING after attempt 1/3 for ~10 minutes, PR_PENDING was already removed, and the process was gone at the next check with no retry lines and no summary -- so the exit path taken (EOF on stdin, a non-Y answer, an error) is NOT established from the log. What is established: a detached run cannot answer the prompt, the remedy for that pull failure is the documented tracker-mutation -> ff-pull -> recover sequence, and the branch cleanup never ran (the local feature branch is still present). Fix: `[[ -t 0 ]] || REPLY=n` before every `read -p` in scripts/auto-pr (or a --yes flag), print the remedy and exit 1 non-interactively; and stash pending .ops around the post-merge pull the way the pre-rebase step already does."  # fd14
    fields: {}  # fd14
- op: discuss  # 986f
