  set:  # b963
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 on PR #743 (WI-suhug), by watching auto-pr sit silent for 15 minutes after \"Note attached\".\n\nSHAPE (LIVE rule 19: a gate can block the work that would activate the mechanism it gates). `auto-pr --tracker-id X` appends a discussion to X (_autopr_append_tracker_discussion, a `tracker discuss`) AFTER the merge but BEFORE it removes `.git/PR_PENDING`. In do_pr, the append (scripts/auto-pr ~2680) precedes cleanup_local (~2685), whose first step is the rm (~2697). The flush path (append ~1873, then _autopr_flush_cleanup's rm ~1895) and the already-merged path (~922, then cleanup_local) have the same order. --detach does not change it, because the watcher child runs the same tail.\n\nThat `tracker discuss` runs `_maybe_auto_sync` (tracker cli.py ~3331). When pending ops are over the threshold (80, sync.py ~872), it sees PR_PENDING and polls for up to `_SYNC_PR_WAIT_TIMEOUT` = 900 s (~3298, wait loop ~3413-3428) for the file to clear. auto-pr is the process that will clear it, and auto-pr is blocked on the child. Observed on 09-03: the child `hypergumbo-tracker discuss WI-suhug... Merged as PR #743` sat in hrtimer_nanosleep for 900 s with no subprocess. Then the sync was SKIPPED (not run), the discuss returned, and auto-pr proceeded. Every `--tracker-id` run whose pending ops are over the threshold pays 15 minutes and then does NOT sync. The pending ops ride on the next mutation.\n\nWHY IT IS NOT A RACE BUT A DESIGN COLLISION. Each gate is correct on its own. The tracker must not merge a sync PR under a feature PR mid-CI, and auto-pr must hold PR_PENDING until its post-merge reconcile is done. The collision is that auto-pr performs a tracker MUTATION inside its own gate.\n\nFIX OPTIONS (pick one):\n  (a) tracker package, non-governance: `_maybe_auto_sync` skips the wait at once, with a one-line notice, when the PR_PENDING holder is an ANCESTOR of the current process. PR_PENDING holds no PID: auto-pr writes the PR number, \"preparing\" or \"detached\" into it. So this must walk the /proc ppid chain looking for auto-pr, not compare a PID from the file.\n  (b) scripts/auto-pr, a GOVERNANCE file (needs_human_review): move the `--tracker-id` discuss to AFTER the PR_PENDING removal, so the mutation runs ungated and auto-sync can fire normally. This is cleaner, because the sync then actually happens.\nEither way, pin it with a test: `_maybe_auto_sync` with PR_PENDING present, held by its own caller, must return in < 1 s.\n\nSECOND FINDING (same 09-03 run), PARTLY FIXED. The post-merge `git pull` failed on incoming tracker-sync commits whose ops files were still pending locally, and reached an interactive `read -p \"Retry?\"` that a detached run cannot answer. Fixed by 7359007100 (2026-09-15): the prompt only runs under `[[ -t 0 ]]` (~2743), and all post-merge housekeeping runs through _autopr_post_merge, so it cannot restate the exit code. Still open: nothing stashes pending .ops around that pull (~2705); the printed hint (~2753) says `git pull origin <base> && git branch -D <branch>` rather than `scripts/tracker reconcile`; and the --squash confirmation `read -p` (~2785) has no tty guard.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # b963
